# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hand-authored PTX implementing the same cooperative-tiled 2D convolution
# algorithm as the reference CuTe/CUDA kernel:
#   - 16x16 spatial output tile per block (256 threads)
#   - OC_TILE = 16 output channels per block
#   - shared memory caches an input patch (with halo) and a weight slice
#     for the current input channel, reused across the whole spatial tile
#
# Optimization applied: double-buffered (ping-pong) shared-memory staging of
# the input/weight tiles using sm_89-supported cp.async instructions. The
# tile for input-channel (ic+1) is asynchronously prefetched into the
# "next" shared-memory buffer while the CTA computes using the already
# resident "current" buffer, overlapping global-memory latency with FMA
# throughput and reducing the number of bar.sync barriers per iteration.
